(2423989, 331502, 22939, '<td valign="top">So, after two years of being a user on this site, only voting at some challenges once in a while and browsing around... I finally took part in a challenge! Why? Because I just got a digital camera for the first time about a month ago.  (Maybe I should have gotten one while I still lived in Iceland, seems like taking pictures there is the way to go...)<br/>I don''t know anything at all about photography really.  I don''t know what words like contrast and saturation mean, have no idea what impact it will have on a shot to change the ISO number, no clue how to edit a pic other then crop and resize and so on... But! I''m here to learn that.  I''ll have to do some reading and experimenting but hopefully I''ll learn something before I give up on this hobby :P<br/>I knew this was not really a good picture when I entered it but I wanted just to try to take part in a challenge, didn''t really care much about the outcome :)  I expected it to place a little bit higher though, maybe around 150th place? :P<br/> <br/>Anyways, thanks a lot for the comments, I really appreciate them! :)<br/> <br/>bfox2: one day I''ll be able to fully understand your comment but at the moment I''m too much of a n00b :P Thanks a lot though, I''m sure it will help later on to get such detailed comments!<br/> <br/>joycamp: Thank you so much for the comment, it''s nice to know that my photo touched someone :) (unless the tears were because my photo was so awful that it was pain to look at it ;P )<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-05-17 06:14:37.</i></td>', 'So, after two years of being a user on this site, only voting at some challenges once in a while and browsing around... I finally took part in a challenge! Why? Because I just got a digital camera for the first time about a month ago.  (Maybe I should have gotten one while I still lived in Iceland, seems like taking pictures there is the way to go...)I don''t know anything at all about photography really.  I don''t know what words like contrast and saturation mean, have no idea what impact it will have on a shot to change the ISO number, no clue how to edit a pic other then crop and resize and so on... But! I''m here to learn that.  I''ll have to do some reading and experimenting but hopefully I''ll learn something before I give up on this hobby :PI knew this was not really a good picture when I entered it but I wanted just to try to take part in a challenge, didn''t really care much about the outcome :)  I expected it to place a little bit higher though, maybe around 150th place? :P Anyways, thanks a lot for the comments, I really appreciate them! :) bfox2: one day I''ll be able to fully understand your comment but at the moment I''m too much of a n00b :P Thanks a lot though, I''m sure it will help later on to get such detailed comments! joycamp: Thank you so much for the comment, it''s nice to know that my photo touched someone :) (unless the tears were because my photo was so awful that it was pain to look at it ;P )', '2006-05-17 07:10:23.000000', '2006-05-17 07:14:37.000000', 0),
